hi i'm genevieve aaron o'brien some of  my friends call me erin o'brien and  other friends call me geo and today i'm  making geo's post pop two of my  signature flavors i'm gonna make the  curio and unicorn union i am a  conceptual performance artist which  means i have advanced degrees in make  believe which also means i make  performances  out of whatever i like and in this case  i made popcorn um each of these popcorns  is inspired by friends and post-colonial  ideas so to me queer cuisine is in the  context of queer the verb to trouble to  make different to subvert the dominant  paradigm if we think about popcorn as  one of the oldest snacks dating back  three to four thousand years how can we  make that different how can we flip the  script on popcorn how can we take what  we think of as a common snack that  everybody recognizes and try savory  flavors and unexpected pairings curio uh  is meant to sound like curio so the idea  is it's uh where indian curry actually  dominates english cheddar for a little  reverse colonization everyone's familiar  with cheese popcorn and who doesn't love  cheese popcorn but if we think about  postcoloniality and where the colonial  empire has been subverted then we  actually have a place where curry can be  the dominant flavor and it actually  pairs really well with english cheddar  it's very hard to find chinese chives  dehydrated in the market in fact if you  find them i'd be really impressed but  you can make your own dried herbs not to  worry just take fresh chinese chives and  go ahead and leave the door open on the  lowest temperature about 200 for about  30 minutes and then you can close the  door and it'll take about an hour to two  hours for those chives to crisp up  unicorn union is actually inspired by my  friend ilokin my buddy diem they wanted  to surprise their boo with a little  present for their birthday and they  actually commissioned this popcorn and  so i wanted to do something that  represented her personality so of course  it has a little bit of nutritional yeast  because you know what's a queer without  a little nutrition and it has a little  bit of lemongrass  and lavender because of course we all  need to relax a little bit and a little  pink peppercorn because well it just  looks like glitter and we can all use a  little extra queer glitter in our life  you know as a conceptual performance  artist i like to talk about big ideas  but i do that through food i use food as  my medium i can't actually paint and you  don't want me to paint i can't draw but  i can express concepts and ideas through  the food and i think food touches us in  a way that it evokes something right you  have to take a risk in order to  experience it it's very different than  standing in in front of a framed  two-dimensional artwork and so for me  being able to use food as a way to  explore these ideas of identity and home  and even queerness is a really powerful  medium to share a story oh yes  you
 

